WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:06.560
Health-CUA asks whether AI agents can do real clinical work inside an electronic health record.

00:07.260 --> 00:14.420
Each agent gets the same task on the same patient record, through the API, our screens, or OpenMRS.

00:15.120 --> 00:17.956
On screen, the agent works like a person.

00:17.956 --> 00:21.761
It reads the chart, clicks, types, and signs the order.

00:22.461 --> 00:28.941
OpenMRS is an independent open source medical record system, used in clinics around the world.

00:29.641 --> 00:34.081
We tested 19 models on 39 real specialist consultations.

00:34.781 --> 00:40.101
Most of the strongest models complete at least as many tasks on screen as through the API.

00:40.801 --> 00:43.441
Memory decides success on screen.

00:43.441 --> 00:49.441
With only its last three screenshots, Claude Sonnet 5.5 solves 1% of tasks.

00:49.441 --> 00:51.601
With its full history, 77%.

00:52.301 --> 00:57.902
In OpenMRS, the same agents complete 16 to 19 points fewer tasks.

00:58.602 --> 01:04.322
We also tested the grader, with scripts that order correctly, leave orders out, or order everything.

01:05.022 --> 01:09.782
Health-CUA. The leaderboard, the paper and the code are on the project page.
